{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdNzxkjiJpkvVtCRMbm4W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XSf4cbYjTUjst9BUfF5Qkv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.1WoNKe/SOLUTION.md","content":"# SOLUTION\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:\n\n1. **`get` did not count as a \"use\".** It read the entry out of the\n   `OrderedDict` but never moved it to the end, so the recency order only ever\n   reflected insertions. A key that was read repeatedly could still be the next\n   one evicted. Fixed by calling `move_to_end(key)` on a successful (non-expired)\n   lookup.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on every insert once full, even for existing keys.** The\n   capacity check ran before looking at whether the key was already present, so\n   updating a key in a full cache dropped the least-recently-used *other* entry\n   and left the cache under capacity. Fixed by only evicting when the key is not\n   already in the cache.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":22615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4983777c-55ce-4921-88b2-3430ceda5fe5","uuid":"a3a26b0b-7266-4418-b767-46e4dbc92129","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:19:10.056Z","request_id":"req_011CdNzxk6X1a9AzQ2UFGQtj"}
